WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.000
Model your first six words.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.000
The most helpful thing you can do
is use the board yourself.

3
00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:10.500
V.O.I.C.E. starts with six words
a child needs every day:

4
00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:14.800
help, stop, eat, drink,
bathroom and more.

5
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:17.400
Tap the word as you say it.

6
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:21.400
At snack: "Time to eat."

7
00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:27.600
Pouring juice: "More?"

8
00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:32.500
Use everyday routines.

9
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:36.800
Meals, the bathroom, play time and getting dressed
all have a place for these words.

10
00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:41.200
Don't make your child copy you.

11
00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:45.800
Just show how it works, the way you'd talk to a baby
long before they talk back.

12
00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:48.600
Treat every tap as talking.

13
00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:53.300
If your child taps "more," give more,
even if it looks like an accident.

14
00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:57.300
Keep the iPad close.
A voice only helps if it's within reach.

15
00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:00.000
V.O.I.C.E. A free AAC app for children
who are new to AAC.
